     1→# Turnstile: API Specification
     2→
     3→**Project:** Turn-Centric Cognitive Interface
     4→**Component:** Backend API
     5→**Status:** Draft
     6→**Last Updated:** December 2025
     7→
     8→---
     9→
    10→## 1. Purpose
    11→
    12→This document defines the backend API that powers Turnstile. The API follows these principles:
    13→
    14→- **REST + WebSocket hybrid** - REST for CRUD, WebSocket for real-time
    15→- **JSON-driven** - All state is JSON, frontend is a renderer
    16→- **Stateless requests** - Server doesn't store request context
    17→- **Idempotent operations** - Safe to retry failed requests
    18→
    19→---
    20→
    21→## 2. Architecture Overview
    22→
    23→```
    24→┌─────────────┐     HTTP/REST      ┌─────────────┐
    25→│   Client    │◀──────────────────▶│   Backend   │
    26→│  (Browser)  │                    │   Server    │
    27→│             │     WebSocket      │             │
    28→│             │◀──────────────────▶│             │
    29→└─────────────┘                    └─────────────┘
    30→                                          │
    31→                                          ▼
    32→                                   ┌─────────────┐
    33→                                   │   LLM API   │
    34→                                   │  (Claude)   │
    35→                                   └─────────────┘
    36→```
    37→
    38→---
    39→
    40→## 3. Base URL
    41→
    42→```
    43→Production:  https://api.carousel.example.com/v1
    44→Development: http://localhost:3001/v1
    45→```
    46→
    47→---
    48→
    49→## 4. Authentication
    50→
    51→### 4.1 Token Format
    52→
    53→```
    54→Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
    55→```
    56→
    57→### 4.2 Token Payload
    58→
    59→```typescript
    60→interface JWTPayload {
    61→  sub: string;           // User ID
    62→  email: string;
    63→  iat: number;           // Issued at
    64→  exp: number;           // Expires at
    65→}
    66→```
    67→
    68→### 4.3 Authentication Endpoints
    69→
    70→#### POST /auth/login
    71→
    72→```typescript
    73→// Request
    74→interface LoginRequest {
    75→  email: string;
    76→  password: string;
    77→}
    78→
    79→// Response
    80→interface LoginResponse {
    81→  token: string;
    82→  refreshToken: string;
    83→  expiresIn: number;     // Seconds
    84→  user: User;
    85→}
    86→```
    87→
    88→#### POST /auth/refresh
    89→
    90→```typescript
    91→// Request
    92→interface RefreshRequest {
    93→  refreshToken: string;
    94→}
    95→
    96→// Response
    97→interface RefreshResponse {
    98→  token: string;
    99→  expiresIn: number;
   100→}
   101→```
   102→
   103→---
   104→
   105→## 5. Session Endpoints
   106→
   107→### 5.1 List Sessions
   108→
   109→#### GET /sessions
   110→
   111→```typescript
   112→// Query parameters
   113→interface ListSessionsQuery {
   114→  limit?: number;        // Default: 20, Max: 100
   115→  offset?: number;       // Default: 0
   116→  sort?: "created" | "updated";
   117→  order?: "asc" | "desc";
   118→}
   119→
   120→// Response
   121→interface ListSessionsResponse {
   122→  sessions: SessionSummary[];
   123→  total: number;
   124→  limit: number;
   125→  offset: number;
   126→}
   127→
   128→interface SessionSummary {
   129→  id: string;
   130→  title: string;
   131→  mode: SessionMode;
   132→  cardCount: number;
   133→  createdAt: string;
   134→  updatedAt: string;
   135→}
   136→```
   137→
   138→### 5.2 Create Session
   139→
   140→#### POST /sessions
   141→
   142→```typescript
   143→// Request
   144→interface CreateSessionRequest {
   145→  title?: string;
   146→  mode?: SessionMode;
   147→  contextPersonaId?: string;
   148→  contextDocumentIds?: string[];
   149→  contextDomains?: string[];
   150→}
   151→
   152→// Response
   153→interface CreateSessionResponse {
   154→  session: SessionState;
   155→}
   156→```
   157→
   158→### 5.3 Get Session
   159→
   160→#### GET /sessions/:sessionId
   161→
   162→```typescript
   163→// Response
   164→interface GetSessionResponse {
   165→  state: ApplicationState;  // Full application state (see json_schema.md)
   166→}
   167→```
   168→
   169→### 5.4 Update Session
   170→
   171→#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId
   172→
   173→```typescript
   174→// Request
   175→interface UpdateSessionRequest {
   176→  title?: string;
   177→  mode?: SessionMode;
   178→}
   179→
   180→// Response
   181→interface UpdateSessionResponse {
   182→  session: SessionState;
   183→}
   184→```
   185→
   186→### 5.5 Delete Session
   187→
   188→#### DELETE /sessions/:sessionId
   189→
   190→```typescript
   191→// Response
   192→interface DeleteSessionResponse {
   193→  success: boolean;
   194→}
   195→```
   196→
   197→---
   198→
   199→## 6. Message Endpoints
   200→
   201→### 6.1 Send Message
   202→
   203→#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/messages
   204→
   205→```typescript
   206→// Request
   207→interface SendMessageRequest {
   208→  content: string;
   209→  attachments?: Attachment[];
   210→}
   211→
   212→interface Attachment {
