# Turnstile: API Specification

**Project:** Turn-Centric Cognitive Interface
**Component:** Backend API
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Purpose

This document defines the backend API that powers Turnstile. The API follows these principles:

- **REST + WebSocket hybrid** - REST for CRUD, WebSocket for real-time
- **JSON-driven** - All state is JSON, frontend is a renderer
- **Stateless requests** - Server doesn't store request context
- **Idempotent operations** - Safe to retry failed requests

---

## 2. Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────┐     HTTP/REST      ┌─────────────┐
│   Client    │◀──────────────────▶│   Backend   │
│  (Browser)  │                    │   Server    │
│             │     WebSocket      │             │
│             │◀──────────────────▶│             │
└─────────────┘                    └─────────────┘
                                          │
                                          ▼
                                   ┌─────────────┐
                                   │   LLM API   │
                                   │  (Claude)   │
                                   └─────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Base URL

```
Production:  https://api.carousel.example.com/v1
Development: http://localhost:3001/v1
```

---

## 4. Authentication

### 4.1 Token Format

```
Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
```

### 4.2 Token Payload

```typescript
interface JWTPayload {
  sub: string;           // User ID
  email: string;
  iat: number;           // Issued at
  exp: number;           // Expires at
}
```

### 4.3 Authentication Endpoints

#### POST /auth/login

```typescript
// Request
interface LoginRequest {
  email: string;
  password: string;
}

// Response
interface LoginResponse {
  token: string;
  refreshToken: string;
  expiresIn: number;     // Seconds
  user: User;
}
```

#### POST /auth/refresh

```typescript
// Request
interface RefreshRequest {
  refreshToken: string;
}

// Response
interface RefreshResponse {
  token: string;
  expiresIn: number;
}
```

---

## 5. Session Endpoints

### 5.1 List Sessions

#### GET /sessions

```typescript
// Query parameters
interface ListSessionsQuery {
  limit?: number;        // Default: 20, Max: 100
  offset?: number;       // Default: 0
  sort?: "created" | "updated";
  order?: "asc" | "desc";
}

// Response
interface ListSessionsResponse {
  sessions: SessionSummary[];
  total: number;
  limit: number;
  offset: number;
}

interface SessionSummary {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  mode: SessionMode;
  cardCount: number;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

### 5.2 Create Session

#### POST /sessions

```typescript
// Request
interface CreateSessionRequest {
  title?: string;
  mode?: SessionMode;
  contextPersonaId?: string;
  contextDocumentIds?: string[];
  contextDomains?: string[];
}

// Response
interface CreateSessionResponse {
  session: SessionState;
}
```

### 5.3 Get Session

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Response
interface GetSessionResponse {
  state: ApplicationState;  // Full application state (see json_schema.md)
}
```

### 5.4 Update Session

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateSessionRequest {
  title?: string;
  mode?: SessionMode;
}

// Response
interface UpdateSessionResponse {
  session: SessionState;
}
```

### 5.5 Delete Session

#### DELETE /sessions/:sessionId

```typescript
// Response
interface DeleteSessionResponse {
  success: boolean;
}
```

---

## 6. Message Endpoints

### 6.1 Send Message

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/messages

```typescript
// Request
interface SendMessageRequest {
  content: string;
  attachments?: Attachment[];
}

interface Attachment {
  type: "file" | "image" | "url";
  content: string;       // Base64 for files, URL for URLs
  name?: string;
  mimeType?: string;
}

// Response (initial)
interface SendMessageResponse {
  cardId: string;
  status: "streaming" | "complete";
}
```

**Note:** This endpoint initiates streaming. The actual AI response arrives via WebSocket.

### 6.2 Get Message History

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId/messages

```typescript
// Query parameters
interface GetMessagesQuery {
  branchId?: string;     // Default: active branch
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
}

// Response
interface GetMessagesResponse {
  cards: TurnCard[];
  total: number;
}
```

---

## 7. Card Endpoints

### 7.1 Update Card

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateCardRequest {
  title?: string;
  collapsed?: boolean;
  tags?: string[];
}

// Response
interface UpdateCardResponse {
  card: TurnCard;
}
```

### 7.2 Delete Card

#### DELETE /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId

```typescript
// Response
interface DeleteCardResponse {
  success: boolean;
  affectedCards: string[];  // IDs of cards renumbered
}
```

### 7.3 Convert Card

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/cards/:cardId/convert

```typescript
// Request
interface ConvertCardRequest {
  to: "task" | "document" | "github-issue" | "whitepaper-seed" | "summary";
  options?: ConvertOptions;
}

interface ConvertOptions {
  includeUserMessage?: boolean;
  includeCode?: boolean;
  format?: "markdown" | "plain";
}

// Response
interface ConvertCardResponse {
  artifact: Artifact;
}

interface Artifact {
  type: string;
  content: string;
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;
}
```

---

## 8. Branch Endpoints

### 8.1 Create Branch

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/branches

```typescript
// Request
interface CreateBranchRequest {
  name: string;
  fromCardId: string;    // Branch point
}

// Response
interface CreateBranchResponse {
  branch: Branch;
}
```

### 8.2 Switch Branch

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/branches/:branchId/activate

```typescript
// Response
interface SwitchBranchResponse {
  state: ApplicationState;  // Full state with new branch
}
```

### 8.3 List Branches

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId/branches

```typescript
// Response
interface ListBranchesResponse {
  branches: Branch[];
  activeBranchId: string;
}
```

---

## 9. Thread Endpoints

### 9.1 Create Thread

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/threads

```typescript
// Request
interface CreateThreadRequest {
  title?: string;
  fromCardId?: string;   // Optional: create from existing card
}

// Response
interface CreateThreadResponse {
  thread: ThreadState;
}
```

### 9.2 Send Thread Message

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/threads/:threadId/messages

```typescript
// Request
interface SendThreadMessageRequest {
  content: string;
}

// Response
interface SendThreadMessageResponse {
  cardId: string;
  status: "streaming" | "complete";
}
```

### 9.3 Update Thread

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId/threads/:threadId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateThreadRequest {
  title?: string;
  state?: "active" | "minimized" | "closed";
  isPinned?: boolean;
  position?: ThreadPosition;
}

// Response
interface UpdateThreadResponse {
  thread: ThreadState;
}
```

### 9.4 Promote Thread Content

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/threads/:threadId/promote

```typescript
// Request
interface PromoteThreadRequest {
  cardIds?: string[];     // Specific cards, or omit for entire thread
  insertPosition: "end" | "after-selected" | number;
  generateSummary?: boolean;
}

// Response
interface PromoteThreadResponse {
  promotedCards: TurnCard[];
  newCarouselState: CarouselState;
}
```

---

## 10. Context Endpoints

### 10.1 List Personas

#### GET /personas

```typescript
// Response
interface ListPersonasResponse {
  personas: Persona[];
}

interface Persona {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description: string;
  domains: string[];
  isDefault: boolean;
}
```

### 10.2 List Documents

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId/documents

```typescript
// Response
interface ListDocumentsResponse {
  documents: Document[];
}

interface Document {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  type: "file" | "url" | "knowledge-base";
  status: "pinned" | "active" | "available" | "muted";
  size?: number;
  excerpt?: string;
}
```

### 10.3 Add Document

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/documents

```typescript
// Request
interface AddDocumentRequest {
  type: "file" | "url";
  content: string;       // Base64 for file, URL for URL
  name?: string;
}

// Response
interface AddDocumentResponse {
  document: Document;
}
```

### 10.4 Update Document Status

#### PATCH /sessions/:sessionId/documents/:documentId

```typescript
// Request
interface UpdateDocumentRequest {
  status: "pinned" | "active" | "available" | "muted";
}

// Response
interface UpdateDocumentResponse {
  document: Document;
}
```

---

## 11. Search Endpoints

### 11.1 Search Conversation

#### GET /sessions/:sessionId/search

```typescript
// Query parameters
interface SearchQuery {
  q: string;
  scope?: "current" | "all-sessions" | "knowledge";
  limit?: number;
}

// Response
interface SearchResponse {
  results: SearchResult[];
  total: number;
}

interface SearchResult {
  type: "card" | "memory" | "knowledge";
  id: string;
  sessionId?: string;
  title: string;
  excerpt: string;
  relevance: number;
  timestamp: string;
}
```

---

## 12. Export Endpoints

### 12.1 Export Session

#### POST /sessions/:sessionId/export

```typescript
// Request
interface ExportRequest {
  format: "json" | "markdown" | "pdf";
  includeThreads?: boolean;
  includeBranches?: boolean;
  branchId?: string;     // Specific branch, or omit for all
}

// Response
interface ExportResponse {
  downloadUrl: string;
  expiresAt: string;
}
```

---

## 13. WebSocket API

### 13.1 Connection

```
wss://api.carousel.example.com/v1/ws?token=<jwt_token>
```

### 13.2 Message Format

```typescript
interface WSMessage {
  type: WSMessageType;
  payload: unknown;
  timestamp: string;
  correlationId?: string;  // Links response to request
}

type WSMessageType =
  // Client → Server
  | "PING"
  | "SUBSCRIBE"
  | "UNSUBSCRIBE"
  | "ACTION"

  // Server → Client
  | "PONG"
  | "STATE_UPDATE"
  | "STREAM_START"
  | "STREAM_CHUNK"
  | "STREAM_END"
  | "ERROR";
```

### 13.3 Subscription

```typescript
// Subscribe to session updates
{
  "type": "SUBSCRIBE",
  "payload": {
    "sessionId": "sess_abc123"
  }
}

// Response
{
  "type": "STATE_UPDATE",
  "payload": {
    "state": { /* ApplicationState */ }
  }
}
```

### 13.4 Streaming Response

When a message is sent, the AI response streams via WebSocket:

```typescript
// Stream start
{
  "type": "STREAM_START",
  "payload": {
    "cardId": "card_007",
    "sessionId": "sess_abc123"
  }
}

// Stream chunks (multiple)
{
  "type": "STREAM_CHUNK",
  "payload": {
    "cardId": "card_007",
    "content": "The carousel architecture ",
    "index": 0
  }
}

{
  "type": "STREAM_CHUNK",
  "payload": {
    "cardId": "card_007",
    "content": "treats each turn as a card...",
    "index": 1
  }
}

// Stream end
{
  "type": "STREAM_END",
  "payload": {
    "cardId": "card_007",
    "card": { /* Complete TurnCard */ }
  }
}
```

### 13.5 Action Dispatch

Client can dispatch actions via WebSocket:

```typescript
// Client sends
{
  "type": "ACTION",
  "payload": {
    "sessionId": "sess_abc123",
    "action": {
      "type": "SELECT_CARD",
      "payload": { "index": 3 }
    }
  },
  "correlationId": "req_123"
}

// Server responds
{
  "type": "STATE_UPDATE",
  "payload": {
    "quadrants": { /* Updated quadrant state */ }
  },
  "correlationId": "req_123"
}
```

---

## 14. Error Handling

### 14.1 Error Response Format

```typescript
interface ErrorResponse {
  error: {
    code: string;
    message: string;
    details?: Record<string, unknown>;
  };
}
```

### 14.2 Error Codes

| Code | HTTP Status | Description |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `AUTH_REQUIRED` | 401 | Missing or invalid token |
| `AUTH_EXPIRED` | 401 | Token expired |
| `FORBIDDEN` | 403 | Not authorized for resource |
| `NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Resource not found |
| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400 | Invalid request body |
| `RATE_LIMITED` | 429 | Too many requests |
| `LLM_ERROR` | 502 | Upstream LLM failed |
| `INTERNAL_ERROR` | 500 | Server error |

### 14.3 Example Error

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Invalid request body",
    "details": {
      "field": "content",
      "reason": "Content cannot be empty"
    }
  }
}
```

---

## 15. Rate Limiting

### 15.1 Limits

| Endpoint Category | Limit |
|-------------------|-------|
| Authentication | 10/min |
| Read operations | 100/min |
| Write operations | 30/min |
| Message send | 20/min |
| WebSocket messages | 60/min |

### 15.2 Rate Limit Headers

```
X-RateLimit-Limit: 100
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 87
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1701878400
```

---

## 16. Health & Status

### GET /health

```typescript
interface HealthResponse {
  status: "healthy" | "degraded" | "unhealthy";
  version: string;
  uptime: number;
  services: {
    database: "up" | "down";
    llm: "up" | "down";
    cache: "up" | "down";
  };
}
```

---

## 18. API Versioning

- Version is in URL path: `/v1/...`
- Breaking changes increment major version
- Old versions supported for 6 months after deprecation
- Deprecation warnings in `X-API-Deprecation` header

---

## 19. CORS Configuration

```
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://carousel.example.com
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Authorization, Content-Type
Access-Control-Max-Age: 86400
```

---

## 20. Client SDK Patterns

### 20.1 TypeScript Client

```typescript
class CarouselClient {
  constructor(baseUrl: string, token: string);

  // Sessions
  listSessions(query?: ListSessionsQuery): Promise<ListSessionsResponse>;
  createSession(req: CreateSessionRequest): Promise<CreateSessionResponse>;
  getSession(sessionId: string): Promise<GetSessionResponse>;
  deleteSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void>;

  // Messages
  sendMessage(sessionId: string, content: string): Promise<SendMessageResponse>;
  onStreamChunk(callback: (chunk: StreamChunk) => void): void;

  // WebSocket
  connect(): Promise<void>;
  subscribe(sessionId: string): void;
  dispatch(action: Action): void;
  onStateUpdate(callback: (state: Partial<ApplicationState>) => void): void;
}
```

### 20.2 Usage Example

```typescript
const client = new CarouselClient("https://api.carousel.example.com/v1", token);

// Connect WebSocket
await client.connect();

// Create session
const { session } = await client.createSession({ title: "New Chat" });

// Subscribe to updates
client.subscribe(session.id);

// Handle state updates
client.onStateUpdate((state) => {
  renderUI(state);
});

// Send message
await client.sendMessage(session.id, "Hello, world!");

// Handle streaming
client.onStreamChunk((chunk) => {
  appendToCard(chunk.cardId, chunk.content);
});
```

---

